<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sheikhdom%20of%20Sharjah.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sheikhdom of Sharjah</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain deposes Sheikh Saqr bin Sultan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/indonesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indonesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indonesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A failed coup is followed by the mass killing of alleged communists</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/malaysia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Malaysia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Malaysia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Singapore is separated from the federation on 9 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/civil-rights-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Civil%20rights%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Civil rights movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Selma to Montgomery marches lead to the Voting Rights Act</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/city-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/City-state.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>City-state</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Singapore leaves the Federation of Malaysia and becomes an independent city-state</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/one-party-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/One-party%20state.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>One-party state</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tanzania becomes a one-party state by law, with rival candidates of the ruling party in most constituencies</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Expelled from Malaysia, Singapore becomes an independent republic on 9 August, with Lee Kuan Yew as prime minister and Yusof bin Ishak as president.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 11 November the Cabinet of Rhodesia issues a unilateral declaration of independence from the United Kingdom; Governor Sir Humphrey Gibbs dismisses Ian Smith and his ministers, who ignore him.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 12 November United Nations Security Council Resolution 216 calls on all states not to recognise 'this illegal racist minority regime in Southern Rhodesia'.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dead-sea-scrolls"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dead%20Sea%20Scrolls.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dead Sea Scrolls</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The collection moved to the newly built Shrine of the Book in Jerusalem</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/armenian-ssr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Armenian%20SSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Armenian SSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 24 April thousands demonstrate in Yerevan on the 50th anniversary of the Armenian genocide; the memorial at Tsitsernakaberd follows in 1967</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Cambodia%20(1953-1970).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Relations with the United States break off, and North Vietnamese forces are allowed permanent bases in Cambodia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/winston-churchill"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Winston%20Churchill.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Winston Churchill</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Churchill dies in London and is given a state funeral</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/mohenjo-daro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mohenjo-daro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mohenjo-daro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The last major excavations, led by George Dales, end and further excavation is banned because of weathering damage</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/lhasa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lhasa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lhasa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Tibet Autonomous Region is established and Lhasa becomes its capital</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/cape-town"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Cape%20Town.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Cape Town</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">District Six is declared a white-only area and its housing is demolished</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/santo-domingo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Santo%20Domingo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Santo Domingo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Fighting between Constitucionalistas and United States troops ends with 2,850 Dominicans and 44 American servicemen dead</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/abu-simbel"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Abu%20Simbel.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Abu Simbel</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first block was lifted out of the Great Temple on 21 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/martin-luther-king-jr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Martin%20Luther%20King%20Jr..png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Martin Luther King Jr.</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Leads marchers to the Edmund Pettus Bridge in Selma and speaks at the end of the march to Montgomery</span></li></ul></section>
